Kernel layouts and file formats follow, and were checked against, the GGUF
format and llama.cpp (MIT License, Copyright the ggml authors) and PrismML's
Bonsai 2 formats PQ2_0 and PTQ1_0. No runtime code from those projects is
included.

`crates/peregrine-core/src/unicode_data.rs` is generated by
`scripts/gen-unicode-tables.py` from llama.cpp's `src/unicode-data.cpp`, which is
MIT licensed (Copyright the ggml authors) and generated in turn from the Unicode
Character Database. It is data, not code: the WordPiece tokenizer must agree with
llama.cpp code point for code point, so the category, case-mapping and
accent-stripping tables are transcribed rather than re-derived from a different
Unicode version. The tokenizer goldens under `crates/peregrine-core/tests/fixtures/`
are llama.cpp's own output for the same files.
